course: dictionary
lesson: 3892
title: Freshly and what it tells us
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word freshly tells you that something happened only a moment ago. It usually comes before a word like made, baked, washed or painted, and that word shows the action is finished. «A freshly blown-out candle can relight through its smoke» means the candle was put out just now, so it is still hot and its wax gas is still there.
explain: Freshly means very recently, or only just. «Freshly baked bread» is bread that came out of the oven a short time ago, so it is warm and new. «Freshly cut grass» is grass that was cut only a little while back.
explain: Freshly also warns you about safety. «Freshly painted» means the paint may still be wet, so do not touch it. Always look at the words around freshly: they show whether something is new, clean or still wet.
fact: Freshly means very recently, or only just.
fact: Freshly usually comes before a past participle such as made, baked, washed or painted.
fact: «Freshly baked bread» means bread that has only just come out of the oven.
fact: «Freshly painted» means the paint may still be wet, so do not touch it.
fact: A good check is to swap in only just and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The shop sells freshly squeezed orange juice.» What does freshly mean here? | *Only just squeezed | Very cheap | Kept in the fridge for a year | Sweet and sticky
exercise: «Mind the wall, it is freshly painted.» What should you do? | Lean on it to test it | Paint over it to help it dry | *Keep your hands off it, because the paint may still be wet | Lick it to check
exercise: «Freshly cut grass» tells you something about the grass. What does it tell you? | *It was cut only a short time ago | It is long, dry and brown | It will never be cut | It has been cut every day for years
test: «The bakers placed freshly baked rolls in the window.» What does freshly mean? | *Only just baked | Frozen solid | Burnt black | Very old and hard
test: «The candle is freshly blown out.» What does this tell you? | It has never been lit | It is a new candle still in its box | It was lit ten years ago | *It was put out only a moment ago
exam: «Freshly painted» is a warning sign. What should you do when you see it? | Touch it to check if it is dry | Paint over it to make it stronger | Read the sign aloud to the paint | *Wait until it is dry and do not touch it
